.TH MYTOP 1 "November 2026" "mytop 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mytop \- terminal system monitor with CPU, memory, GPU, network, disk and sensor graphs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mytop
[\fB\-i\fR \fIMS\fR]
[\fB\-\-bench\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mytop
is an interactive, top\-style monitor for Linux. It shows braille history
graphs and live statistics for the CPU, memory, every GPU, network
interfaces, disks and hardware sensors, plus a sortable process table that
includes per\-process GPU utilisation and video memory.
.PP
GPUs from three vendors are supported:
.TP
.B NVIDIA
through NVML (\fIlibnvidia\-ml.so.1\fR, shipped with the proprietary
driver). The library is loaded at run time; without it mytop still runs and
simply shows no NVIDIA data.
.TP
.B Intel
(i915 and xe drivers) through sysfs, hwmon, RC6/gt\-idle residency, the
i915 query ioctl and DRM fdinfo.
.TP
.B AMD
(amdgpu driver) through sysfs, hwmon and DRM fdinfo.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interval " " \fIMS\fR
Refresh interval in milliseconds (100\(en10000, default 1000).
.TP
.B \-\-bench
Run ten refreshes without a user interface, print the average time each
collector took and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage message and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR q ", " Esc ", " Ctrl\-C
Quit.
.TP
.B s
Cycle the process sort column (cpu, mem, gpu, pid, name).
.TP
.B r
Reverse the sort order.
.TP
.BR c ", " m ", " g ", " p ", " n
Sort processes by CPU, memory, GPU, PID or name.
.TP
.BR Up ", " Down ", " PgUp ", " PgDn ", " Home ", " End
Move the process selection.
.TP
.B k
Send SIGTERM to the selected process (asks for confirmation).
.TP
.B K
Send SIGKILL to the selected process (asks for confirmation).
.TP
.BR + ", " \-
Increase or decrease the refresh interval by 250 ms.
.TP
.B Space
Pause or resume updates.
.TP
.BR 1 \(en 7
Show or hide the cpu, mem, gpu, net, disk, sensors and procs panels.
.SH PERMISSIONS
mytop runs as an ordinary user. A few readings need more privileges:
.IP \(bu 2
Per\-process GPU usage for Intel and AMD comes from
\fI/proc/<pid>/fdinfo\fR, which a normal user can read only for their own
processes. Run mytop as root to see every process. The GPU panel shows
\(lqown procs only\(rq when this applies.
.IP \(bu 2
Intel VRAM \(lqused\(rq from the i915 query ioctl requires CAP_PERFMON (root);
otherwise VRAM used is the sum of the processes that are visible.
.IP \(bu 2
Opening the Intel render node (\fI/dev/dri/renderD*\fR) requires membership
of the \fBrender\fR group, which desktop users normally have.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /proc/stat, /proc/meminfo, /proc/net/dev, /proc/diskstats
CPU, memory, network and disk counters.
.TP
.I /proc/<pid>/stat, /proc/<pid>/cmdline, /proc/<pid>/fdinfo/*
Process statistics and DRM client usage.
.TP
.I /sys/class/hwmon/*
Temperature and fan sensors.
.TP
.I /sys/class/drm/card*
GPU discovery and AMD/Intel statistics.
.TP
.I /sys/firmware/memmap
Installed RAM.
.SH NOTES
Motherboard temperatures and fan speeds appear only when a Super\-I/O
sensor driver such as \fBnct6775\fR or \fBit87\fR is loaded; see
.BR sensors\-detect (8).
